    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nmini.files\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nTrying to access file which is used by another process crashes preview function with message:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nError executing vim.schedule lua callback: ...ppData/Local/nvim-data/lazy/mini.nvim/lua/mini/files.lua:2067: bad argument #1 to 'fs_read' (number expected, got nil)\r\nstack traceback:\r\n[C]: in function 'fs_read'\r\n...ppData/Local/nvim-data/lazy/mini.nvim/lua/mini/files.lua:2067: in function 'update_fun'\r\n...ppData/Local/nvim-data/lazy/mini.nvim/lua/mini/files.lua:2009: in function 'buffer_update'\r\n...ppData/Local/nvim-data/lazy/mini.nvim/lua/mini/files.lua:1802: in function 'view_ensure_proper'\r\n...ppData/Local/nvim-data/lazy/mini.nvim/lua/mini/files.lua:1569: in function 'explorer_refresh_depth_window'\r\n...ppData/Local/nvim-data/lazy/mini.nvim/lua/mini/files.lua:1351: in function 'explorer_refresh'\r\n...ppData/Local/nvim-data/lazy/mini.nvim/lua/mini/files.lua:1876: in function 'fn'\r\nvim/_editor.lua:351: in function <vim/_editor.lua:350>\r\n```\r\n\r\n```lua\r\n-- module config\r\nMiniFiles.setup({\r\n  mappings = {\r\n    close = \"q\",\r\n    go_in = \"<Right>\",\r\n    go_in_plus = \"L\",\r\n    go_out = \"<Left>\",\r\n    go_out_plus = \"H\",\r\n    reset = \"<BS>\",\r\n    reveal_cwd = \"@\",\r\n    show_help = \"g?\",\r\n    synchronize = \"=\",\r\n    trim_left = \"<\",\r\n    trim_right = \">\",\r\n  },\r\n  windows = {\r\n    -- Maximum number of windows to show side by side\r\n    max_number = math.huge,\r\n    -- Whether to show preview of file/directory under cursor\r\n    preview = true,\r\n    -- Width of focused window\r\n    width_focus = 50,\r\n    -- Width of non-focused window\r\n    width_nofocus = 15,\r\n    -- Width of preview window\r\n    width_preview = 25,\r\n  },\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\n\r\n### Neovim version\r\n\r\nNVIM v0.10.1 Build type: Release LuaJIT 2.1.1713484068, Windows 11\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\n1. Use windows 11\r\n2. Install mini.files\r\n3. Enable preview\r\n4. Try to access file with blocked(?) handle (i.e. NTUSER.DAT in home dir)\r\n\r\n```C:\\Users\\Username> cat .\\NTUSER.DAT\r\nGet-Content: The process cannot access the file 'C:\\Users\\Username\\NTUSER.DAT' because it is being used by another process.```\r\n\r\n\r\n### Expected behavior\r\n\r\nNo error - preferably access denied message or similar.\r\n\r\n### Actual behavior\r\n\r\nError message:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nError executing vim.schedule lua callback: ...ppData/Local/nvim-data/lazy/mini.nvim/lua/mini/files.lua:2067: bad argument #1 to 'fs_read' (number expected, got nil)                                                                                        \r\nstack traceback:                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    [C]: in function 'fs_read'\r\n...ppData/Local/nvim-data/lazy/mini.nvim/lua/mini/files.lua:2067: in function 'update_fun'\r\n...ppData/Local/nvim-data/lazy/mini.nvim/lua/mini/files.lua:2009: in function 'buffer_update'\r\n...ppData/Local/nvim-data/lazy/mini.nvim/lua/mini/files.lua:1802: in function 'view_ensure_proper'\r\n...ppData/Local/nvim-data/lazy/mini.nvim/lua/mini/files.lua:1569: in function 'explorer_refresh_depth_window'\r\n...ppData/Local/nvim-data/lazy/mini.nvim/lua/mini/files.lua:1351: in function 'explorer_refresh'\r\n...ppData/Local/nvim-data/lazy/mini.nvim/lua/mini/files.lua:1876: in function 'fn'\r\nvim/_editor.lua:351: in function <vim/_editor.lua:350>                                                                                                                                                                                             Press ENTER or type command to continue     \r\n```",
