            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "@marcinmdev, would you mind checking if the following patch fixes your use case?\r\n\r\n```diff\r\ndiff --git a/lua/mini/files.lua b/lua/mini/files.lua\r\nindex 41a49b8..c050060 100644\r\n--- a/lua/mini/files.lua\r\n+++ b/lua/mini/files.lua\r\n@@ -2061,6 +2061,10 @@ H.buffer_update_directory = function(buf_id, path, opts)\r\n end\r\n \r\n H.buffer_update_file = function(buf_id, path, opts)\r\n+  if vim.fn.filereadable(path) == 0 then\r\n+    H.set_buflines(buf_id, { '-Non-read-file' .. string.rep('-', opts.windows.width_preview) })\r\n+    return {}\r\n+  end\r\n   -- Determine if file is text. This is not 100% proof, but good enough.\r\n   -- Source: https://github.com/sharkdp/content_inspector\r\n   local fd = vim.loop.fs_open(path, 'r', 1)\r\n```\r\n\r\nIt's just `vim.fn.filereadable()` is the preferred method in 'mini.nvim' to check if the file is readable.",
